/-!
# Exact success probability of the DL and CDH self-reductions in a fixed group

Fix an additive commutative group `G` that is a `ZMod q`-module and an element `g : G`, as in
`CslibFrontier/Crypto/Computational/DiffieHellman/Finite.lean`; the textbook `g^a` is `a • g`.
[BonehShoup2023], Section 10.5.1, turns an adversary `A` that finds the discrete logarithm of a
random group element with probability `ε` into an algorithm `B` that finds the discrete logarithm
of every element with probability `ε` (Theorem 10.2), and Exercise 10.6 asks for the same for CDH.
This module writes these algorithms as programs that call `A` once per attempt, and computes their
exact output probabilities in one fixed group. This layer has no cost model, so it does not state
that `B` is efficient, which Theorem 10.2 also claims, nor the consequence over a group family,
that worst-case hardness of the discrete logarithm implies average-case hardness. Both are in
`CslibFrontier/Crypto/Computational/DiffieHellman/SelfReduction/Family.lean`, for word-level
adversaries over a `PrimeOrderGroupFamily`.

Write `ε = dlAdvantage q g A`, the success probability of `A` in the discrete-logarithm experiment
for `g`. Footnote 1 of the book (p. 411) fixes the group and generator in the same way. The book
draws a uniform input `u` and asks for `Dlog_g(u)`; the experiment draws a uniform exponent `a` and
asks for `a`, which is the same when `g` generates a group of order `q`.

* `dlRerandomize q g A u` masks `u` as `u + σ • g` for a uniform exponent `σ`, runs `A` on it and
  subtracts `σ` from the answer. On `u = α • g` it returns `α` with probability exactly `ε`.
* `dlSelfReduce q g A k u` makes at most `k` such attempts and returns the first answer `x` with
  `x • g = u`, or `none` (`OracleComp.retry`). `dlSelfReduce q g A 1` is the book's `B` (p. 412)
  with `none` for `fail`.
* `cdhSelfReduce q g A u v` masks both inputs, as `u + ρ • g` and `v + τ • g`, runs `A`, and
  removes the three cross terms of `((α + ρ) * (β + τ)) • g`. Exercise 10.6 gives no construction;
  this one is ours. It applies the one-sided map of Exercise 10.5, `ũ = g^ρ · u` with
  `[ũ, v] = [u, v] · v^ρ`, to both inputs. Masking one input does not suffice: the test file has an
  adversary for which one-sided masking succeeds with probability `1` or `0` depending on `v`.

Exercise 10.5 itself needs no lemma here. Part (a) is `uniformOfFintype_bind_smul_add` with
`uniformOfFintype_bind_smul`, and part (b) is the identity
`((α + ρ) * β) • g = (α * β) • g + ρ • (β • g)`, one step of `module`.

The book takes `G` cyclic of prime order `q`, generated by `g`. The results below need neither
primality nor a generator. The exact equalities for `k` attempts assume instead that `c ↦ c • g` is
injective on `ZMod q` (that `g` has order `q`), and every result except soundness concerns an input
of the form `α • g`; in the book's setting both hold for every input. Testing an answer needs
`DecidableEq G`. Probabilities are values of `ProbComp.eval` in `ℝ≥0∞`, and `ε : ℝ≥0` is coerced.

## Main definitions

* `Cslib.Crypto.dlRerandomize`: one masked call of a discrete-logarithm adversary.
* `Cslib.Crypto.dlSelfReduce`: at most `k` masked calls, returning the first checked answer.
* `Cslib.Crypto.cdhSelfReduce`: one call of a CDH adversary with both inputs masked.

## Main results

* `Cslib.Crypto.eval_dlRerandomize_smul_apply`: one masked call on `α • g` returns `α` with
  probability `ε`.
* `Cslib.Crypto.smul_eq_of_mem_support_dlSelfReduce`: `dlSelfReduce` returns `none` or a discrete
  logarithm of its input, for every input (Theorem 10.2: "outputs fail or `Dlog_g(u)`").
* `Cslib.Crypto.eval_dlSelfReduce_one_smul_some`: one attempt on `α • g` returns `α` with
  probability `ε` (the probability in Theorem 10.2).
* `Cslib.Crypto.eval_dlSelfReduce_smul_none_le`: `k` attempts all fail with probability at most
  `(1 - ε) ^ k`. When `c ↦ c • g` is injective, `Cslib.Crypto.eval_dlSelfReduce_smul_none` and
  `Cslib.Crypto.eval_dlSelfReduce_smul_some` give the exact probabilities `(1 - ε) ^ k` of failing
  and `1 - (1 - ε) ^ k` of returning `α`.
* `Cslib.Crypto.eval_dlSelfReduce_smul_none_le_exp_mul`,
  `Cslib.Crypto.eval_dlSelfReduce_smul_none_le_exp`,
  `Cslib.Crypto.one_sub_exp_le_eval_dlSelfReduce_smul_some`: the iteration remark after
  Theorem 10.2. With `n ⌈1 / ε⌉` attempts the failure probability is at most `exp (-n)`, and the
  probability of returning `α` is at least `1 - exp (-n)`.
* `Cslib.Crypto.eval_cdhSelfReduce_smul_apply`: on `(α • g, β • g)`, `cdhSelfReduce` returns
  `(α * β) • g` with probability equal to the CDH advantage of `A` (Exercise 10.6).

## References

* [D. Boneh, V. Shoup, *A Graduate Course in Applied Cryptography*][BonehShoup2023], Section
  10.5.1: Theorem 10.2, the remark after it and its proof (pp. 411–412); Exercises 10.5 and 10.6
  (pp. 424–425).
-/

public section

namespace Cslib.Crypto

open Probability
open scoped NNReal ENNReal

variable {G : Type} [AddCommGroup G] (q : ℕ) [NeZero q] [Module (ZMod q) G] (g : G)

/-! ### The programs -/

/-- One masked call of a discrete-logarithm adversary `A` on `u`: draw a uniform exponent `σ`, run
`A` on `u + σ • g` (the textbook `u · g^σ`) and subtract `σ` from its answer. This is the
algorithm `B` in the proof of [BonehShoup2023], Theorem 10.2 (p. 412), without its final test. -/
@[expose] noncomputable def dlRerandomize (A : G → ProbComp (ZMod q)) (u : G) :
    ProbComp (ZMod q) := do
  let σ ← $ᵗ ZMod q
  let α₁ ← A (u + σ • g)
  return α₁ - σ

/-- At most `k` masked calls of `A` on `u` (`dlRerandomize`), returning the first answer `x` with
`x • g = u`, or `none` when all `k` answers fail this test. `dlSelfReduce q g A 1` is the algorithm
`B` in the proof of [BonehShoup2023], Theorem 10.2 (p. 412), with `none` for its output `fail`. The
book tests `g^α₁ = u · g^σ` and then outputs `α₁ - σ`; this program tests `(α₁ - σ) • g = u`,
which is the same test by `sub_smul`. -/
@[expose] noncomputable def dlSelfReduce [DecidableEq G] (A : G → ProbComp (ZMod q)) (k : ℕ)
    (u : G) : ProbComp (Option (ZMod q)) :=
  OracleComp.retry (fun x : ZMod q => x • g = u) (dlRerandomize q g A u) k

/-- One call of a CDH adversary `A` on `(u, v)` with both inputs masked: draw uniform exponents `ρ`
and `τ`, run `A` on `(u + ρ • g, v + τ • g)` and subtract `τ • u + ρ • v + (ρ * τ) • g` from its
answer. When `u = α • g` and `v = β • g`, the correct answer for the masked inputs is
`((α + ρ) * (β + τ)) • g`, and the subtraction leaves `(α * β) • g`.

[BonehShoup2023], Exercise 10.6 (p. 425) asks for such an algorithm without giving one; this
construction is ours. It has no `fail` output: as the remark after the exercise notes, under DDH
there is no way to recognize a correct answer. -/
@[expose] noncomputable def cdhSelfReduce (A : G → G → ProbComp G) (u v : G) : ProbComp G := do
  let ρ ← $ᵗ ZMod q
  let τ ← $ᵗ ZMod q
  let w ← A (u + ρ • g) (v + τ • g)
  return w - τ • u - ρ • v - (ρ * τ) • g

/-! ### One attempt -/

private theorem coe_dlAdvantage (A : G → ProbComp (ZMod q)) :
    (dlAdvantage q g A : ℝ≥0∞) = ProbComp.eval (dlExperiment q g A) true :=
  Game.coe_succProbability_ennreal _

/-- One masked call on `α • g` returns `α` with probability exactly the discrete-logarithm advantage
of `A`, whatever `α`: substituting `a = α + σ`, a bijection of `ZMod q`, turns the event into
`A (a • g) = a` for uniform `a`. The substitution is on exponents, not group elements, so no
hypothesis on `G`, `q` or `g` is needed. -/
theorem eval_dlRerandomize_smul_apply (A : G → ProbComp (ZMod q)) (α : ZMod q) :
    ProbComp.eval (dlRerandomize q g A (α • g)) α = ProbComp.eval (dlExperiment q g A) true := by
  have hlaw : ProbComp.eval (dlRerandomize q g A (α • g)) =
      (PMF.uniformOfFintype (ZMod q)).bind fun a =>
        (ProbComp.eval (A (a • g))).bind fun α₁ => PMF.pure (α₁ - (a - α)) := by
    rw [← PMF.uniformOfFintype_bind_equiv (Equiv.addLeft α)]
    simp only [dlRerandomize, ProbComp.eval_bind, ProbComp.eval_pure, ProbComp.eval_uniform,
      Equiv.coe_addLeft, add_smul, add_sub_cancel_left]
  have hevent (a x : ZMod q) : α = x - (a - α) ↔ true = decide (x = a) := by
    rw [eq_comm (a := true), decide_eq_true_iff]
    constructor <;> intro h <;> linear_combination -h
  simp only [hlaw, dlExperiment, ProbComp.eval_bind, ProbComp.eval_pure, ProbComp.eval_uniform,
    PMF.bind_apply, PMF.pure_apply]
  refine tsum_congr fun a => ?_
  congr 1
  refine tsum_congr fun x => ?_
  congr 1
  congr 1
  exact propext (hevent a x)

/-- **Soundness of the discrete-logarithm self-reduction.** Every answer `some x` that
`dlSelfReduce` can return is a discrete logarithm of its input: `x • g = u`. This is the claim of
[BonehShoup2023], Theorem 10.2 (pp. 411–412), that `B` outputs either `fail` or `Dlog_g(u)`, here
for every `u` and `k` and with no hypothesis on the group. -/
theorem smul_eq_of_mem_support_dlSelfReduce [DecidableEq G] {A : G → ProbComp (ZMod q)} {k : ℕ}
    {u : G} {x : ZMod q} (hx : some x ∈ (ProbComp.eval (dlSelfReduce q g A k u)).support) :
    x • g = u := by
  rw [ProbComp.support_eval] at hx
  exact (OracleComp.mem_supportWith_retry hx).1

/-- **The probability in [BonehShoup2023], Theorem 10.2** (pp. 411–412), in a fixed group: on input
`α • g`, one attempt returns `α` with probability exactly `ε = dlAdvantage q g A`. The theorem's
claim that `B` is efficient is not stated here; the family-level form is
`Cslib.Crypto.PrimeOrderGroupFamily.le_toOuterMeasure_dlSelfReduceRetryAdversary_one`, and
`Cslib.Crypto.PrimeOrderGroupFamily.isPPTOn_dlSelfReduceRetryAdversary` certifies its program.
The book takes `G` cyclic of prime order `q` with generator `g`, where every input is `α • g` for
its discrete logarithm `α`; this needs neither hypothesis. -/
theorem eval_dlSelfReduce_one_smul_some [DecidableEq G] (A : G → ProbComp (ZMod q))
    (α : ZMod q) :
    ProbComp.eval (dlSelfReduce q g A 1 (α • g)) (some α) = dlAdvantage q g A := by
  have h := OracleComp.evalWith_retry_some (fun x : ZMod q => x • g = α • g)
    (dlRerandomize q g A (α • g)) ProbComp.unifOracle 1 α
  simp only [Finset.range_one, Finset.sum_singleton, pow_zero, mul_one, ite_true] at h
  rw [coe_dlAdvantage, ← eval_dlRerandomize_smul_apply q g A α]
  exact h

/-! ### Repeated attempts -/

/-- `k` attempts on `α • g` all fail with probability at most `(1 - ε) ^ k`, with no hypothesis on
the group. The bound is an equality when `c ↦ c • g` is injective
(`eval_dlSelfReduce_smul_none`); otherwise an attempt can also succeed with another discrete
logarithm of `α • g`. -/
theorem eval_dlSelfReduce_smul_none_le [DecidableEq G] (A : G → ProbComp (ZMod q)) (k : ℕ)
    (α : ZMod q) :
    ProbComp.eval (dlSelfReduce q g A k (α • g)) none ≤ (1 - (dlAdvantage q g A : ℝ≥0∞)) ^ k := by
  refine OracleComp.evalWith_retry_none_le _ _ _
    (Probability.PMF.toOuterMeasure_compl_le_one_sub _ {x | x • g = α • g} ?_) k
  rw [coe_dlAdvantage, ← eval_dlRerandomize_smul_apply q g A α,
    ← PMF.toOuterMeasure_apply_singleton]
  exact MeasureTheory.OuterMeasure.mono _ (Set.singleton_subset_iff.2 rfl)

/-- When `c ↦ c • g` is injective, one attempt on `α • g` fails with probability exactly
`1 - ε`. -/
private theorem toOuterMeasure_eval_dlRerandomize_not
    (hg : Function.Injective fun c : ZMod q => c • g) (A : G → ProbComp (ZMod q)) (α : ZMod q) :
    (ProbComp.eval (dlRerandomize q g A (α • g))).toOuterMeasure {x | ¬x • g = α • g} =
      1 - (dlAdvantage q g A : ℝ≥0∞) := by
  have hsum := Probability.PMF.toOuterMeasure_add_compl_ennreal
    (ProbComp.eval (dlRerandomize q g A (α • g))) {α}
  rw [PMF.toOuterMeasure_apply_singleton, eval_dlRerandomize_smul_apply, ← coe_dlAdvantage]
    at hsum
  have hset : {x : ZMod q | ¬x • g = α • g} = ({α} : Set (ZMod q))ᶜ :=
    Set.ext fun _ => not_congr hg.eq_iff
  rw [hset]
  exact ENNReal.eq_sub_of_add_eq ENNReal.coe_ne_top (by rw [add_comm]; exact hsum)

/-- When `c ↦ c • g` is injective on `ZMod q` (that is, `g` has order `q`), `k` attempts on `α • g`
all fail with probability exactly `(1 - ε) ^ k`. -/
theorem eval_dlSelfReduce_smul_none [DecidableEq G]
    (hg : Function.Injective fun c : ZMod q => c • g) (A : G → ProbComp (ZMod q)) (k : ℕ)
    (α : ZMod q) :
    ProbComp.eval (dlSelfReduce q g A k (α • g)) none = (1 - (dlAdvantage q g A : ℝ≥0∞)) ^ k := by
  rw [← toOuterMeasure_eval_dlRerandomize_not q g hg A α]
  exact OracleComp.evalWith_retry_none _ _ _ k

/-- When `c ↦ c • g` is injective, `dlSelfReduce` on `α • g` returns `none` or `some α`. -/
private theorem eval_dlSelfReduce_smul_some_add_none [DecidableEq G]
    (hg : Function.Injective fun c : ZMod q => c • g) (A : G → ProbComp (ZMod q)) (k : ℕ)
    (α : ZMod q) :
    ProbComp.eval (dlSelfReduce q g A k (α • g)) (some α) +
      ProbComp.eval (dlSelfReduce q g A k (α • g)) none = 1 := by
  set p := ProbComp.eval (dlSelfReduce q g A k (α • g)) with hp
  have hc : p.toOuterMeasure {none}ᶜ = p (some α) := by
    rw [← PMF.toOuterMeasure_apply_singleton]
    refine p.toOuterMeasure_apply_eq_of_inter_support_eq (Set.ext fun y => ?_)
    cases y with
    | none => simp
    | some x =>
      simp only [Set.mem_inter_iff, Set.mem_compl_iff, Set.mem_singleton_iff, reduceCtorEq,
        not_false_eq_true, true_and, Option.some.injEq]
      exact ⟨fun hs => ⟨hg (smul_eq_of_mem_support_dlSelfReduce q g (hp ▸ hs)), hs⟩, And.right⟩
  rw [← hc, ← PMF.toOuterMeasure_apply_singleton, add_comm]
  exact Probability.PMF.toOuterMeasure_add_compl_ennreal p {none}

/-- When `c ↦ c • g` is injective, `k` attempts on `α • g` return `α` with probability exactly
`1 - (1 - ε) ^ k`, the probability in the remark after [BonehShoup2023], Theorem 10.2 (p. 412). -/
theorem eval_dlSelfReduce_smul_some [DecidableEq G]
    (hg : Function.Injective fun c : ZMod q => c • g) (A : G → ProbComp (ZMod q)) (k : ℕ)
    (α : ZMod q) :
    ProbComp.eval (dlSelfReduce q g A k (α • g)) (some α) =
      1 - (1 - (dlAdvantage q g A : ℝ≥0∞)) ^ k := by
  rw [← eval_dlSelfReduce_smul_none q g hg A k α]
  exact ENNReal.eq_sub_of_add_eq (PMF.apply_ne_top _ _)
    (eval_dlSelfReduce_smul_some_add_none q g hg A k α)

/-- `k` attempts on `α • g` all fail with probability at most `exp (-(k ε))`, with no hypothesis on
the group or on `ε`. -/
theorem eval_dlSelfReduce_smul_none_le_exp_mul [DecidableEq G] (A : G → ProbComp (ZMod q))
    (k : ℕ) (α : ZMod q) :
    (ProbComp.eval (dlSelfReduce q g A k (α • g)) none).toReal ≤
      Real.exp (-(k * (dlAdvantage q g A : ℝ))) := by
  have h1 : dlAdvantage q g A ≤ 1 := Game.succProbability_le_one _
  calc (ProbComp.eval (dlSelfReduce q g A k (α • g)) none).toReal
      ≤ ((1 - (dlAdvantage q g A : ℝ≥0∞)) ^ k).toReal :=
        ENNReal.toReal_mono (ENNReal.pow_ne_top (ENNReal.sub_ne_top ENNReal.one_ne_top))
          (eval_dlSelfReduce_smul_none_le q g A k α)
    _ = (1 - (dlAdvantage q g A : ℝ)) ^ k := by
        rw [ENNReal.toReal_pow, ENNReal.toReal_sub_of_le (by exact_mod_cast h1) ENNReal.one_ne_top,
          ENNReal.toReal_one, ENNReal.coe_toReal]
    _ ≤ Real.exp (-(k * (dlAdvantage q g A : ℝ))) :=
        Real.one_sub_pow_le_exp (by exact_mod_cast h1) le_rfl

/-- `n ≤ n ⌈1 / ε⌉ ε` for `0 < ε`. -/
private theorem natCast_le_mul_ceil_inv_mul {ε : ℝ≥0} (hε : 0 < ε) (n : ℕ) :
    (n : ℝ) ≤ ((n * ⌈ε⁻¹⌉₊ : ℕ) : ℝ) * ε := by
  have hc : (ε : ℝ)⁻¹ ≤ ⌈ε⁻¹⌉₊ := by exact_mod_cast Nat.le_ceil ε⁻¹
  have hpos : (0 : ℝ) < ε := by exact_mod_cast hε
  calc (n : ℝ) = n * ((ε : ℝ)⁻¹ * ε) := by rw [inv_mul_cancel₀ hpos.ne', mul_one]
    _ ≤ n * (⌈ε⁻¹⌉₊ * ε) := by gcongr
    _ = ((n * ⌈ε⁻¹⌉₊ : ℕ) : ℝ) * ε := by push_cast; ring

/-- **The remark after [BonehShoup2023], Theorem 10.2** (p. 412), failure form: when `0 < ε`,
`n ⌈1 / ε⌉` attempts on `α • g` all fail with probability at most `exp (-n)`. The book leaves
`0 < ε` implicit in the count; here `⌈ε⁻¹⌉₊ = 0` when `ε = 0`, and the test file shows that the
bound then fails. No hypothesis on the group is needed: when the loop does not fail, it returns a
discrete logarithm of `α • g` (`smul_eq_of_mem_support_dlSelfReduce`). -/
theorem eval_dlSelfReduce_smul_none_le_exp [DecidableEq G] (A : G → ProbComp (ZMod q))
    (hε : 0 < dlAdvantage q g A) (n : ℕ) (α : ZMod q) :
    (ProbComp.eval (dlSelfReduce q g A (n * ⌈(dlAdvantage q g A)⁻¹⌉₊) (α • g)) none).toReal ≤
      Real.exp (-(n : ℝ)) :=
  (eval_dlSelfReduce_smul_none_le_exp_mul q g A _ α).trans
    (Real.exp_le_exp.2 (neg_le_neg (natCast_le_mul_ceil_inv_mul hε n)))

/-- **The remark after [BonehShoup2023], Theorem 10.2** (p. 412): when `c ↦ c • g` is injective and
`0 < ε`, `n ⌈1 / ε⌉` attempts on `α • g` return `α` with probability at least `1 - exp (-n)`. The
book writes this as `1 - (1 - ε)^(n⌈1/ε⌉) ≥ 1 - exp(-n)`, whose left side is the exact probability
of `eval_dlSelfReduce_smul_some`. -/
theorem one_sub_exp_le_eval_dlSelfReduce_smul_some [DecidableEq G]
    (hg : Function.Injective fun c : ZMod q => c • g) (A : G → ProbComp (ZMod q))
    (hε : 0 < dlAdvantage q g A) (n : ℕ) (α : ZMod q) :
    1 - Real.exp (-(n : ℝ)) ≤
      (ProbComp.eval (dlSelfReduce q g A (n * ⌈(dlAdvantage q g A)⁻¹⌉₊) (α • g))
        (some α)).toReal := by
  have hsome := ENNReal.eq_sub_of_add_eq (PMF.apply_ne_top _ _)
    (eval_dlSelfReduce_smul_some_add_none q g hg A (n * ⌈(dlAdvantage q g A)⁻¹⌉₊) α)
  rw [hsome, ENNReal.toReal_sub_of_le (PMF.coe_le_one _ _) ENNReal.one_ne_top, ENNReal.toReal_one]
  linarith [eval_dlSelfReduce_smul_none_le_exp q g A hε n α]

/-! ### Computational Diffie–Hellman -/

/-- **The success probability asked for in [BonehShoup2023], Exercise 10.6** (p. 425), in a fixed
group: on every input `(α • g, β • g)`, `cdhSelfReduce` returns the Diffie–Hellman element
`(α * β) • g` with probability exactly the CDH advantage of `A`. The construction is ours, since
the exercise gives none, and its efficiency is not stated here; the family-level form is
`Cslib.Crypto.PrimeOrderGroupFamily.advantage_cdhSelfReduceAdversary_le`, and
`Cslib.Crypto.PrimeOrderGroupFamily.isPPT_cdhSelfReduceAdversary` certifies its program. The book
takes `G` cyclic of prime order `q` with generator `g`; this needs neither hypothesis. -/
theorem eval_cdhSelfReduce_smul_apply [DecidableEq G] (A : G → G → ProbComp G) (α β : ZMod q) :
    ProbComp.eval (cdhSelfReduce q g A (α • g) (β • g)) ((α * β) • g) =
      ProbComp.eval (cdhExperiment q g A) true := by
  -- Substitute `a = α + ρ` and `b = β + τ` in the experiment.
  have hshift (H : ZMod q → ZMod q → PMF Bool) :
      ((PMF.uniformOfFintype (ZMod q)).bind fun a =>
        (PMF.uniformOfFintype (ZMod q)).bind fun b => H a b) =
      (PMF.uniformOfFintype (ZMod q)).bind fun ρ =>
        (PMF.uniformOfFintype (ZMod q)).bind fun τ => H (α + ρ) (β + τ) := by
    rw [← PMF.uniformOfFintype_bind_equiv (Equiv.addLeft α)]
    refine congrArg (PMF.bind _) (funext fun ρ => ?_)
    exact (PMF.uniformOfFintype_bind_equiv (Equiv.addLeft β) (H (α + ρ))).symm
  have hexp : ProbComp.eval (cdhExperiment q g A) =
      (PMF.uniformOfFintype (ZMod q)).bind fun ρ => (PMF.uniformOfFintype (ZMod q)).bind fun τ =>
        (ProbComp.eval (A ((α + ρ) • g) ((β + τ) • g))).bind fun w =>
          PMF.pure (decide (w = ((α + ρ) * (β + τ)) • g)) := by
    simp only [cdhExperiment, ProbComp.eval_bind, ProbComp.eval_pure, ProbComp.eval_uniform]
    exact hshift fun a b => (ProbComp.eval (A (a • g) (b • g))).bind fun w =>
      PMF.pure (decide (w = (a * b) • g))
  have hevent (ρ τ : ZMod q) (w : G) :
      (α * β) • g = w - τ • α • g - ρ • β • g - (ρ * τ) • g ↔
        true = decide (w = ((α + ρ) * (β + τ)) • g) := by
    rw [eq_comm (a := true), decide_eq_true_iff]
    constructor <;> intro h
    · rw [eq_sub_iff_add_eq, eq_sub_iff_add_eq, eq_sub_iff_add_eq] at h
      rw [← h]
      module
    · rw [h]
      module
  simp only [hexp, cdhSelfReduce, ProbComp.eval_bind, ProbComp.eval_pure, ProbComp.eval_uniform,
    PMF.bind_apply, PMF.pure_apply, add_smul]
  refine tsum_congr fun ρ => ?_
  congr 1
  refine tsum_congr fun τ => ?_
  congr 1
  refine tsum_congr fun w => ?_
  congr 1
  congr 1
  exact propext (hevent ρ τ w)

end Cslib.Crypto
